// partial score=0.97 date=2026-09-21
// cl: /DNDEBUG /MD
// ?count@Rva00271AE0Owner@@QAEHXZ  rva=0x00271AE0 size=77
// partial: 78 bytes, 23 non-reloc diffs, 6 differing INSTRUCTIONS (the tail is
// instruction-identical, only shifted by one byte).
//
// NEW this session: the record stride is 12, not 6.  Retail's tail is
//   mov eax,0x2aaaaaab / imul ecx / sar edx,1 / mov eax,edx / shr eax,31 / add eax,edx
// and the `sar edx,1` is the magic-division shift for /12 (0x2AAAAAAB with s=1).
// Every earlier bank divided by 6, dropped `sar edx,1` and therefore computed a
// runtime-wrong count as well as missing a byte.  This body reproduces the whole
// magic-division tail exactly.
//
// Remaining divergence (first at +0x1b): retail keeps the host pointer in EDX for
// the whole body, so the fallback pointer goes to EAX and the final span loads are
// `mov eax,[edx+0x44] / mov ecx,[edx+0x48] / sub ecx,eax`.  MSVC 7.1 instead treats
// `m_host` as a free rematerialisation: it CSEs it into EDX, reuses EDX for the
// fallback pointer, and reloads `[ecx+0x30]` for the span, folding the subtract.
// The choice is binary and stable across every spelling tried:
//   member expression everywhere  -> host = EDX, reloaded at the tail (this file)
//   host cached in ANY named value -> host = EAX and id demoted to ECX (59 diffs)
// where "any named value" covers a plain local, a reference, an inlined
// Host::count() member (host becomes the inlined `this`), a static helper taking
// `const Host *`, and an inlined `distance(first,last)` helper for the span.
// Explicit first/last locals for the span are folded back by the optimiser.
// /O1, /Og /Os, /Ox, /Og /Ot, /Oy-, /G5, /G7, /Oa and /Ob1 were also swept: /O1 and
// /Og /Os collapse the body to 68 bytes, everything else reproduces this file.

